      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start and definitely hits the technical points.\n\nHowever, looking at the completeness metric, the word count is sitting pretty low. I'm worried that if it's this brief, some of the junior devs might hit a wall if they run into a basic issue (like a Docker permission error or a Node version mismatch).\n\nCan you beef this up a bit? Try to expand on the prerequisites and the steps to ensure we're hitting a more substantial word count for the library's reporting. Just keep it professional and technical—avoid just repeating yourself, but definitely add more depth and detail so the score is higher.",
      "source": "evaluator"
