    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded version of the \"Quick Start\" guide:\n\n**Quick Start for SkyLink CLI**\n\nGet your development environment up and running in under 5 minutes!\n\nBefore you begin, ensure that your environment meets the following prerequisites:\n\n1. **Verify Docker installation**: Make sure Docker is installed and running on your machine. If Docker is not installed, you can download and install it from the official Docker website. [https://www.docker.com/get-started](https://www.docker.com/get-started)\n2. **Check Node.js version**: Ensure that your Node.js version is 18 or higher. If you're using a version manager like nvm or a package manager like npm or yarn, verify that your current version meets the system requirements. If you're using an older version, update it by running `npm install -g nvm` and following the installation instructions.\n3. **Set up your shell configuration**: If you're using a shell like bash or zsh, make sure your shell configuration file is set up to allow Docker to run without issues.\n\nOnce you've met the prerequisites, install the SkyLink CLI globally using npm:\n```bash\nnpm install -g skylink-cli\n```\nThis may take a few minutes",
      "source": "target",
